  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "If Annie gave Jacob $\\$20$, then they would have the same amount of money. If Jacob gave Annie $\\$22$, however, then Annie would then have twice as much as Jacob. How much money do they each have?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Annie has $\\$146$ and Jacob has $\\$106$.\n\nModel both transfers with simultaneous equations and solve by substitution.",
      "worked": "Let Annie have $x$ dollars and Jacob have $y$ dollars.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x-20&=y+20\\\\x&=y+40\\\\x+22&=2(y-22)\\\\y+40+22&=2(y-22)\\\\y+62&=2y-44\\\\y&=106\\\\x&=106+40\\\\x&=146\\end{align*}$$\n\nAnnie has $\\$146$ and Jacob has $\\$106$. After the first transfer, each has $\\$126$. After the second transfer, Annie has $\\$168$ and Jacob has $\\$84$, so Annie has twice as much.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 92
  },
